# Cross-OS line-ending policy (D181, ci-cross-os-repair): store AND
# check out LF everywhere. The windows-latest runner defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrote committed text artifacts to CRLF
# at checkout — include_str! then embedded the CRLF bytes and the
# diffharness s*_plan_matches_committed_artifact pins failed on the
# first windows test run (run 33122184098) while the generated plans
# are LF. eol=lf overrides autocrlf on every platform, making the
# byte-exact artifact comparisons OS-invariant. No tracked file
# carries CR in the index (verified: git grep -lI $'\r' HEAD is
# empty at a18d9c3), so no renormalization is needed.
* text=auto eol=lf
